<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.6 percent in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.6 percent in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.6 percent in the week to July 30 over the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said on Thursday. Last week the rise was 5.5 percent. (figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			     Latest week Previous wk year-ago wk</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     22.05	  21.93	20.88</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	    2.61	   2.60	 1.80    --</p>
<p>London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
